{"slug":"valid-parentheses","title":"Valid Parentheses","difficulty":"easy","tags":["string","stack"],"problem_type":"string_parsing","input_pattern":"[()\\[\\]{}]*","statement":"Given a string `s` made only of the characters `(`, `)`, `[`, `]`, `{` and `}`, decide whether it is valid.\n\nA string is valid when every opening bracket is closed by the same kind of bracket, and brackets close in the right order. The empty string is valid.\n\n### Input\nOne line containing `s` (it may be empty).\n\n### Output\n`true` or `false`.\n\n### Constraints\n- 0 \u2264 |s| < 10\u2074\n","limits":{"timeMs":{"cpp":1000,"c":1000,"python":2000},"memoryMb":128},"starterCode":{"cpp":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    getline(cin, s);\n\n    bool ok = true;\n    // TODO\n    cout << (ok ? \"true\" : \"false\") << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n","c":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstatic char s[10005];\n\nint main(void) {\n    if (!fgets(s, sizeof s, stdin)) s[0] = 0;\n    s[strcspn(s, \"\\n\")] = 0;\n\n    int ok = 1;\n    /* TODO */\n    puts(ok ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n    return 0;\n}\n","python":"import sys\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip(\"\\n\")\n\n    ok = True\n    # TODO\n    print(\"true\" if ok else \"false\")\n\nmain()\n"},"tests":[{"args":{"input_string":"()"},"expectedOutput":"true\n","sample":true},{"args":{"input_string":"()[]{}"},"expectedOutput":"true\n","sample":true},{"args":{"input_string":"(]"},"expectedOutput":"false\n","sample":true,"explanation":"The ']' closes a bracket that was opened with '('."},{"args":{"input_string":"([{}])"},"expectedOutput":"true\n","sample":true},{"args":{"input_string":""},"expectedOutput":"true\n","sample":false},{"args":{"input_string":"("},"expectedOutput":"false\n","sample":false},{"args":{"input_string":")("},"expectedOutput":"false\n","sample":false},{"args":{"input_string":"{[]}()[{()}]"},"expectedOutput":"true\n","sample":false},{"args":{"input_stri